 those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 10.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.7 to 6.3. December accounts for 20% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,987 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if awardee A has other contracts. Review contract [1] to see if the amount is unusually close to the limit, which might indicate a pricing strategy rather than a breach.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["ec5hsnkm25TVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D","wpIlyC6wQLfL1rX3q%2FMAPA%3D%3D","9X5JARoIe9XzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}